# <repository name> — local secrets and settings. Copy to `.env` and fill; `.env` is
# git-ignored and never read by Claude (.claude/settings.json denies it). Keys for
# complementary models come from the client organisation through the project lead; the
# Claude Code licence comes from the Project Advisor and needs no key here.
#
# One variable per vendor, named <VENDOR>_API_KEY (optional <VENDOR>_BASE_URL when a
# provider sits in front of several vendors). Code reads them through the project's single
# model helper, never directly.

# --- complementary models (only those a task actually needs)
# <VENDOR>_API_KEY=
# <VENDOR>_BASE_URL=

# --- application (filled after the design phase, from the stack DD; names are the
# CLAUDE.md "Commands" table's)
